Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:05:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the validation layer run, and prove each gate can fail
 (B-44)

Three quality gates this repo documents had never executed: the SHACL
shapes were never run (and, once run, rejected the repo's own example
data with 7 violations because the snorkel and aerial shapes both
targeted every survey event), the competency file held three queries
in one .rq that no engine parses, and robot-profile.yaml replaced
ROBOT's default report profile with two INFO rules so --fail-on ERROR
had run nothing that could fail since 2025.

- SHACL: the two method-specific shapes use a SHACL-core implication
  so their constraints apply only to events of their method; the
  countUnitIRI constraint accepts an IRI node or an xsd:anyURI literal
  until the property is declared with a range. `make shacl-validate`
  runs the shapes over the example data under pyshacl (pinned to
  0.31.0, the newest that resolves against the rdflib pin CI relies
  on). No SHACL-AF on purpose: an engine without it ignores a SPARQL
  target silently and reports a vacuous pass.
- Competency questions: split one per file under
  ontology/sparql/competency/, bodies unchanged; `make
  competency-questions` executes each separately and fails on a parse
  error. All three return zero rows because they name terms the
  ontology does not declare; that is reported, not failed, and recorded
  as a term decision in docs/tech-debt.md.
- ROBOT: robot-profile.yaml is now the default profile from the pinned
  jar with exactly missing_label and missing_definition at INFO. The
  re-enabled duplicate_label check finds gcdfo:WildSalmonPolicy and
  gcdfo:WildSalmonPolicyTheme sharing a label, so `make quality-check`
  fails on main until a label changes; deliberately not silenced.
  scripts/robot-quality-check.sh could not report a failure (set -e
  killed it before its ERROR branch); fixed, and it prints the rows.
- Self-test: `make validation-selftest` (inside `make test`) points
  each gate at a fixture under tests/fixtures/ broken on purpose and
  asserts it fails for the documented reason, including that the
  profile equals the jar's default modulo the two downgrades. Shown to
  go red against the pre-fix shapes and the pre-fix profile.

No ontology term IRI, label or definition is chosen, changed or removed.
ADR-010, CHANGELOG, entrypoints, ROBOT_SETUP and tech-debt updated.

