+### The profile amends the default; it does not replace it
+
+`robot report --profile FILE` **replaces** ROBOT's built-in profile with the
+rules listed in `FILE`. It does not merge them. From 2025 until 2026-09-10
+`robot-profile.yaml` was two lines —
+
+```
+INFO	missing_label
+INFO	missing_definition
+```
+
+— so the report ran exactly two checks, both at a level `--fail-on ERROR`
+cannot fail on, and the sixteen ERROR-level checks in the default profile
+(`duplicate_label`, `illegal_use_of_built_in_vocabulary`,
+`label_whitespace`, `deprecated_class_reference`, `multiple_labels`,
+`missing_ontology_license`, …) never ran at all. The gate was green for
+every commit in that window and could not have been anything else.
+Verified 2026-08-10 (metasalmon hub, queue item B-44), fixed 2026-09-10.
+
+`robot-profile.yaml` is now `report_profile.txt` copied out of the pinned
+`tools/robot.jar` (ROBOT 1.9.8, 32 rules) with exactly two changes:
+
+| rule | default | here | why |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `missing_label` | ERROR | INFO | this ontology labels SKOS concepts with `skos:prefLabel`, which ROBOT does not read as a label; every `gcdfo:` subject carries one |
+| `missing_definition` | WARN | INFO | definitions live in `iao:0000115` / `skos:definition`, which ROBOT does not read; WARN would not fail the build either, INFO is the level the repo had already chosen |
+
+Nothing else differs, and that is enforced: `scripts/validation-selftest.sh`
+(inside `make test`) extracts the default profile from the jar and fails if
+`robot-profile.yaml` differs from it by anything other than those two
+lines — including after a ROBOT upgrade that changes the default, which is
+the signal to re-derive the file. ROBOT rejects comment lines in a profile
+(`REPORT LEVEL ERROR '# …' is not a valid reporting level`), so the file
+itself cannot say any of this; this section and the header of
+`scripts/robot-quality-check.sh` are where it is said.
+
+To re-derive after a ROBOT bump:
+
+```bash
+python3 -c 'import zipfile; print(zipfile.ZipFile("tools/robot.jar").read("report_profile.txt").decode())' \
+  | sed -e 's/^ERROR\tmissing_label/INFO\tmissing_label/' -e 's/^WARN\tmissing_definition/INFO\tmissing_definition/' \
+  > robot-profile.yaml
+```
+
+The self-test also proves the gate can fail: `tests/fixtures/robot/duplicate-label.ttl`
+must exit 1 under this profile with `duplicate_label` as its only ERROR rule.
+
